WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.176
Since 2005,

2
00:00:01.176 --> 00:00:02.740
any citizen can ask a

3
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.123
public office for information.

4
00:00:05.123 --> 00:00:06.250
And the law sets a

5
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.971
clock on the answer.

6
00:00:08.302 --> 00:00:10.452
The office must reply within

7
00:00:10.452 --> 00:00:11.406
30 days.

8
00:00:11.406 --> 00:00:12.967
Or within 48 hours,

9
00:00:12.967 --> 00:00:14.528
if a person's life or

10
00:00:14.528 --> 00:00:16.505
liberty is involved.

11
00:00:16.856 --> 00:00:18.593
Section 4 asks offices to

12
00:00:18.593 --> 00:00:21.524
publish information without being asked.

13
00:00:21.524 --> 00:00:23.702
Section 8 lists exemptions,

14
00:00:23.702 --> 00:00:25.672
and Section 24 leaves out

15
00:00:25.672 --> 00:00:27.914
some security agencies.

16
00:00:28.266 --> 00:00:29.800
Use it in GS2 on

17
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.530
transparency and accountability.

18
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.096
The best R-T-I is the

19
00:00:34.096 --> 00:00:36.441
one nobody had to file.

20
00:00:37.121 --> 00:00:38.298
Your turn.

21
00:00:38.298 --> 00:00:39.886
What's the time limit for

22
00:00:39.886 --> 00:00:41.456
life or liberty?
